#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Add eleven opt-in loop, cse, register-allocation, scheduling and alignment rules, first
needed by func_L04_00417308.

-frac2-loop-align-in-loop-only: final's loop alignment goes only to a label inside the loop; a
loop whose body has no label does not pass its alignment to a label after its LOOP_END.
-frac2-la-const-longer-first: local-alloc: of two quantities of a block set from integer
constants with equal reference counts, the longer-lived gets its register first.
-frac2-sched-hoisted-first: before reload, on a full scheduling tie, an insn that loop
invariant motion moved out of a loop goes first.
-frac2-cse-path-11: a cse path may follow 11 jumps instead of 10.
-frac2-loop-move-temps: loop invariant motion may move a conditionally set compiler temporary
(only a user variable or a loop-test register is pinned by the maybe-never/used-before checks).
-frac2-sched-arg-sum-first: before reload, on a full tie between two sets of hard registers, a
register-plus-constant sum goes before a copy of a pseudo.
-frac2-ga-hoisted-var-first: global-alloc: a floating-point user variable whose set was moved
out of a loop counts 3% higher.
-frac2-sched-call-last: before reload, a call heading the ready list issues after the next ready
insn of its cycle when that insn came before the call in the original order.
-frac2-sched-argreg-wait: before reload, a set of an argument register that depends on a
preceding call waits two cycles after it when the call used the register, returns a value, or
the set copies the call's value register (constant loads after a call without a value do not
wait).
-frac2-sched-frame-temp-first: before reload, on a full tie between two frame-address
computations, the one into a compiler temporary goes before the one into a user variable.
-frac2-sched-call-with-arg-copy: before reload, a call with a value that a delayed
(-frac2-sched-argreg-wait) copy of a pseudo into one of its argument registers made ready issues
in the copy's cycle.

The marks of insns moved out of loops (loop.c, read by sched1 and global-alloc) are cleared for
each function. Forced on for every USA v1.01 C unit they change, in
the order above, 6, 810, 528, 20, 398, 1063, 1, 54, 2317, 64 and 6 functions
(-frac2-sched-call-with-arg-copy on top of -frac2-sched-argreg-wait: 2;
-frac2-ga-hoisted-var-first on top of -frac2-sched-hoisted-first: 0). Opt-in per-unit models under the owner's standard of
12 November 2026. Default compilation is unchanged.

Usage: l04_17308_rules.py <gcc directory>
"""
